# Implementation Patch — GPA Transcript Zero Grades Fix (Revised)

## Root Cause (verified against DB, 2026-08-05)

- `syllabus` table: 166 records, **ALL with `academic_year_id = NULL`** (use `effective_from`/`effective_to` instead)
- `threshold` table: 418 records — **332 WITH `academic_year_id` (79.4%)**, only 86 NULL (20.6%)
- Helper `secondary-gpa-report.helper.ts:213` runs `Syllabus.findOne({ academicYearId })` → **always returns null** (syllabus is 100% NULL)
- The guard at line 239-243 (`syllabus && boundaries`) therefore always fails → `calculatePUM` never runs → grades default to '0'
- The `Threshold.findOne({ academicYearId })` lookup is also wrong, but it is NOT the primary blocker
- **Known data gap:** some subjects have a valid ACTIVE threshold but no syllabus record at all — the old guard silently dropped these to '0' even when `avgValue` was valid

**Fix strategy:** replace both direct-FK lookups with `effective_from`/`effective_to` range lookups. Reuse the existing `SyllabusService.findEffectiveForSubjectYear` (syllabus.service.ts:499); add the equivalent on `ThresholdService`. Relax the guard to **threshold-only** so a valid threshold converts grades even when no syllabus matches. No DB migration.

