### Key changes vs. the buggy code

| Before | After |
|--------|-------|
| `Syllabus.findOne({ academicYearId })` — always null | `syllabusService.findEffectiveForSubjectYear(subjectId, academicYearId, thresholdType)` — method already exists (syllabus.service.ts:499) |
| `Threshold.findOne({ academicYearId })` — misses NULL-ay records | `thresholdService.findEffectiveForSubjectYear(...)` — new method (File 1) |
| Dead debug code (`activeYear` split on `[1]`, console.logs) | Removed |
| Guard `syllabus && boundaries` — **syllabus is mandatory**; valid threshold with no syllabus → grade '0' | Guard `boundaries && Object.keys(boundaries).length > 0` — **threshold is sufficient**; syllabus is optional, contributes only `gradeSchema` |
| `syllabus?.gradeSchema` passed to `calculatePUM` | **Kept** — when the syllabus resolves, the schema filters grade keys (A–C, A*–E); when it is null, `gradeSchema` is `undefined` and `getPassingGradeEntries` falls back to `GRADE_ORDER` filtered by the keys in `avgValue` (cambridge-grading.ts:53-69) |

### Removed after this change
- Imports no longer needed: `Syllabus` (line 25), `Threshold` entity (line 24) — verify no other usage before removing

